.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_FLAGS 3 2026-09-12 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_flags \- return stored MPQ file flags.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_flags("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s  *" "archive",
.BI "        uint32_t        " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t       *" "flags"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The function returns the selected member's actual stored block-table flags
in \fIflags\fP. Inspect the public LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_COMPRESS,
LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_IMPLODE, LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_ENCRYPTED,
LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SINGLE, and LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SECTOR_CRC bits for storage
properties. Other stored bits are returned unchanged.
.PP
COMPRESS and IMPLODE describe file storage; individual sectors may fall back
to raw data. Use \fBlibmpq__block_compression\fP() for a sector's effective
method. This query does not read payload data or verify checksums.
.PP
A non-NULL output is initialized to zero before argument validation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, a zero is returned and on error one of the following constants.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
The archive or output pointer is NULL, or the file number is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_files (3),
.BR libmpq__block_compression (3)
